    "details": "<p><strong>Rules:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Team Structure:\n<ul>\n<li>Each team must consist of a minimum of 2 and a maximum of 6 members.</li>\n<li>Participants from different colleges can form a team.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Model Regulations:\n<ul>\n<li>Each team must have its own custom-built drone; exchanging models between teams is strictly prohibited.</li>\n<li>RTF (Ready-To-Fly) models are not allowed, but pre-programmed boards can be used.</li>\n<li>Only one model can be used throughout all competition rounds.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Flight and Conduct Rules:\n<ul>\n<li>No trial attempts are allowed in Round 1, but teams can have a 2-minute trial before Round 2.</li>\n<li>Lifting the drone manually to improve position during any round is not allowed.</li>\n<li>Any failed landing attempt that does not result in a score immediately ends the round.</li>\n<li>The competition organizers and judges hold the final decision on any disputes.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Event Structure:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Round 1:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Teams must fly their drone through 5 circular rings placed at varying heights (between 1 meter to 2.5 meters).</li>\n<li>Each ring carries different points based on difficulty.</li>\n<li>Teams must avoid touching the rings to earn points.</li>\n<li>Skipping a ring results in no points but does not incur a penalty.</li>\n<li>Maximum time for completion: 8 minutes.</li>\n<li>Qualification Criteria: Teams with the highest scores will advance to Round 2.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Round 2:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Obstacle Navigation: Teams must maneuver through multiple obstacles, which will be disclosed on the spot.</li>\n<li>Payload Task:\n<ul>\n<li>The onboard camera scans a QR code to identify a specific payload.</li>\n<li>If scanning fails, teams can receive the QR details manually but will lose detection points.</li>\n<li>The identified payload must be dropped into a designated area.</li>\n<li>No penalty for unsuccessful drops, but no points are awarded either.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>",
    "end_date": "2026-11-14T19:08:53+05:30",
